Variable Settings
"water level" is an integer with range [0,100]
"coffee beans level" is an integer with range [0,100]
"machine status" is a string with range {READY, BREWING, ERROR} and initial value 'READY'

Scenario 01: brewing starts when sufficient resources are available
Given the system is in its initial state
And the user interface displays information on "machine status" equal to 'READY'
When the user issues a brew request
And the machine has a current "water level", "coffee beans level" such that:
    "water level" is greater than 20 AND
    "coffee beans level" is greater than 10
Then the user interface displays "machine status" equal to 'BREWING'
And the machine serves coffee
And the user interface displays "machine status" equal to 'READY'

Scenario 02: brewing fails when the water level is too low
Given the system is in its initial state
And the user interface displays information on "machine status" equal to 'READY'
When the user issues a brew request
And the machine has a current "water level", "coffee beans level" such that:
    "water level" is lower or equal than 20 OR
    "coffee beans level" is lower or equal than 10
Then the user interface displays "machine status" equal to 'ERROR'

Scenario 03: brewing error recovery
Given the user interface displays information on "machine status" equal to 'ERROR'
When the user does a manual reset
Then the user interface displays "machine status" equal to 'READY'

